1
00:04:25,806 --> 00:04:27,558
Good morning, James.

2
00:04:27,683 --> 00:04:28,851
How are you feeling?

3
00:04:29,059 --> 00:04:30,102
Wait. What?

4
00:04:30,519 --> 00:04:33,331
It's perfectly normal to feel confused.

5
00:04:33,355 --> 00:04:36,901
You just spent 120 years
in suspended animation.

6
00:04:37,526 --> 00:04:38,527
What?

7
00:04:38,861 --> 00:04:40,321
It's okay, James.

8
00:04:40,863 --> 00:04:42,865
- It's Jim.
- Jim.

9
00:04:43,699 --> 00:04:46,660
Just breathe. Everything is okay.

10
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:48,138
Where am I?

11
00:04:48,162 --> 00:04:50,307
You're a passenger on the starship avalon,

12
00:04:50,331 --> 00:04:53,959
the homestead company's
premier interstellar starliner.

13
00:04:55,336 --> 00:04:58,672
We've nearly completed the voyage
from earth to your new home.

14
00:04:59,089 --> 00:05:01,133
The colony world of homestead ii.

15
00:05:02,384 --> 00:05:05,030
A new world. A fresh start.

16
00:05:05,054 --> 00:05:06,615
Room to grow.

17
00:05:06,639 --> 00:05:08,366
Yeah.

18
00:05:08,390 --> 00:05:10,494
The avalon is on final approach.

19
00:05:10,518 --> 00:05:12,662
For the next four months,
you'll enjoy space travel

20
00:05:12,686 --> 00:05:14,563
at its most luxurious.

21
00:05:15,147 --> 00:05:17,626
Food. Fun. Friends.

22
00:05:17,650 --> 00:05:20,069
- My friends.
- That's right, Jim.

23
00:05:20,444 --> 00:05:23,531
<i>The ID band on your wrist is your key
to the wonders of the avalon.</i>

24
00:05:26,158 --> 00:05:27,928
You're in perfect health, Jim.

25
00:05:27,952 --> 00:05:30,496
Let's get you to your cabin,
where you can get some rest.

26
00:05:38,462 --> 00:05:41,340
You may be experiencing
post-hibernation sickness.

27
00:05:43,634 --> 00:05:45,970
Your door will illuminate for you.

28
00:05:49,181 --> 00:05:50,575
Welcome to your cabin,

29
00:05:50,599 --> 00:05:52,994
your home until we make landfall.

30
00:05:53,018 --> 00:05:54,162
Over the next four months,

31
00:05:54,186 --> 00:05:57,064
you'll prepare for your new life
on homestead 1,

32
00:05:57,523 --> 00:06:00,710
meet your fellow passengers,
take skill-building classes,

33
00:06:00,734 --> 00:06:02,611
and learn about colonial living.

34
00:06:03,195 --> 00:06:05,590
You've been assigned to learning group 38

35
00:06:05,614 --> 00:06:08,701
for passengers with engineering
and technical trade skills.

36
00:06:08,993 --> 00:06:11,537
Please scan your ID
to confirm luggage delivery.

37
00:06:13,122 --> 00:06:14,474
Jim.

38
00:06:14,498 --> 00:06:17,167
Please scan your ID
to confirm luggage delivery.

39
00:06:21,714 --> 00:06:26,302
To help you recover from hibernation,
be sure to drink plenty of fluids.

40
00:06:27,970 --> 00:06:30,615
Enjoy the rest of your voyage on the avalon,

41
00:06:30,639 --> 00:06:32,808
a homestead company starship.

42
00:06:35,436 --> 00:06:36,955
Good morning, one and all.

43
00:06:36,979 --> 00:06:39,666
It's a beautiful morning
here on the starship avalon.

44
00:06:39,690 --> 00:06:42,460
Whatever you do, don't get homesick,
get homestead.

45
00:06:42,484 --> 00:06:44,737
Let's start things off
with one of my favorites back on earth.

46
00:06:51,660 --> 00:06:53,078
No.

47
00:06:55,873 --> 00:06:57,499
That's stupid.

48
00:07:01,378 --> 00:07:04,548
Just own it. Own it, Jim.
You got a cool jacket.

49
00:07:18,854 --> 00:07:20,522
Hello, passengers.

50
00:07:21,231 --> 00:07:23,150
Will you all please take a seat.

51
00:07:24,485 --> 00:07:27,505
Welcome, learning group 38.

52
00:07:27,529 --> 00:07:30,199
Your introduction to colonial life.

53
00:07:30,699 --> 00:07:34,453
Earth is a prosperous planet,
the cradle of civilization.

54
00:07:34,870 --> 00:07:39,667
But for many, it's also overpopulated,
overpriced, overrated.

55
00:07:40,376 --> 00:07:42,479
I'm sorry, I think I may be in the wrong...

56
