102
00:10:53,735 --> 00:10:56,738
Homestead ll is the fourth planet
in the bhakti system.

103
00:10:57,114 --> 00:10:59,384
Right. And where are we?

104
00:10:59,408 --> 00:11:02,411
We're in transit from earth to homestead ii.

105
00:11:02,578 --> 00:11:05,390
We will arrive in approximately 90 years.

106
00:11:05,414 --> 00:11:06,432
What?

107
00:11:06,456 --> 00:11:09,894
We arrive at homestead ii
in 90 years, three weeks and one day.

108
00:11:09,918 --> 00:11:11,146
No. Wait.

109
00:11:11,170 --> 00:11:12,814
How long ago did we leave earth?

110
00:11:12,838 --> 00:11:15,299
Approximately 30 years ago.

111
00:11:19,303 --> 00:11:21,638
I woke up too soon.

112
00:11:23,974 --> 00:11:25,076
Hello.

113
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:26,744
How do I send a message to earth?

114
00:11:26,768 --> 00:11:29,205
Interstellar messages are sent by laser array.

115
00:11:29,229 --> 00:11:30,748
This is an expensive service.

116
00:11:30,772 --> 00:11:32,441
- Bite me.
- Happy to help.

117
00:11:35,444 --> 00:11:36,612
Planet and connection?

118
00:11:36,862 --> 00:11:38,780
Earth. The homestead company.

119
00:11:38,989 --> 00:11:43,285
There are 30,826 contacts
listed under homestead company.

120
00:11:43,911 --> 00:11:46,973
I'm emigrating to homestead ll
and I have an emergency.

121
00:11:46,997 --> 00:11:48,266
I have a customer help line.

122
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:49,291
Sounds about right.

123
00:11:49,666 --> 00:11:50,667
Begin message.

124
00:11:52,002 --> 00:11:54,713
Hi. I'm Jim Preston.

125
00:11:55,505 --> 00:11:57,049
I'm a passenger on the avalon.

126
00:11:57,841 --> 00:11:59,259
I...

127
00:12:02,262 --> 00:12:05,158
I think something went wrong
with my hibernation pod.

128
00:12:05,182 --> 00:12:06,618
I woke up too soon.

129
00:12:06,642 --> 00:12:10,371
And I mean, way too soon.

130
00:12:10,395 --> 00:12:13,023
Nobody else is awake, and...

131
00:12:13,607 --> 00:12:15,418
I don't know how to get back to sleep.

132
00:12:15,442 --> 00:12:18,570
And the thing is, there's 90 years to go.

133
00:12:21,823 --> 00:12:24,409
At this rate, I'm...

134
00:12:27,913 --> 00:12:30,374
I'm sorry, I'm trying to fix this.

135
00:12:30,540 --> 00:12:33,460
Maybe I missed something.
I could use a hand.

136
00:12:34,169 --> 00:12:35,504
That's all.

137
00:12:36,338 --> 00:12:37,339
Thank you.

138
00:12:38,966 --> 00:12:40,259
Message sent.

139
00:12:42,427 --> 00:12:43,529
Outstanding.

140
00:12:43,553 --> 00:12:45,847
Message will arrive in 19 years.

141
00:12:46,014 --> 00:12:47,057
Wait, what?

142
00:12:47,266 --> 00:12:49,268
Earliest reply in 55 years.

143
00:12:49,893 --> 00:12:51,853
Fifty-five years?

144
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:54,189
We apologize for the delay.

145
00:12:54,356 --> 00:12:56,817
That will be $6,012.

146
00:13:10,956 --> 00:13:12,624
- Afternoon.
- Man!

147
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:14,793
Is it good to see another face!

148
00:13:15,252 --> 00:13:16,712
Thought I was the only one awake.

149
00:13:16,837 --> 00:13:19,923
Who wants to sleep
on a beautiful day like this?

150
00:13:20,090 --> 00:13:22,926
No, I mean we're in trouble.
We're not supposed to be here.

151
00:13:23,176 --> 00:13:25,053
Well, I won't tell if you don't.

152
00:13:26,263 --> 00:13:27,764
Our little secret.

153
00:13:29,391 --> 00:13:30,684
What can I get for you?

154
00:13:30,892 --> 00:13:31,893
What?

155
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:33,437
You look like a whiskey man.

156
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:35,522
Okay.

157
00:13:40,402 --> 00:13:41,820
You're a robot.

158
00:13:42,571 --> 00:13:44,740
Android. Technically.

159
00:13:47,284 --> 00:13:48,368
Arthur's the name.

160
00:13:49,536 --> 00:13:51,830
- Jim.
- Pleased to meet you, Jim.

161
00:13:57,919 --> 00:13:59,588
How much do you know about this ship?

162
00:14:00,255 --> 00:14:01,607
I don't know.

163
00:14:01,631 --> 00:14:02,716
I know some things.

164
00:14:02,841 --> 00:14:05,278
What do I do
if my hibernation pod malfunctions?

165
00:14:05,302 --> 00:14:07,864
Hibernation pods are fail-safe.

166
00:14:07,888 --> 00:14:09,240
They never malfunction.

167
00:14:09,264 --> 00:14:10,474
Well, I woke up early.

168
00:14:10,849 --> 00:14:12,017
Can't happen.

169
00:14:12,684 --> 00:14:14,579
How long until we get to homestead ii?

170
00:14:14,603 --> 00:14:16,497
About 90 years or so.

171
00:14:16,521 --> 00:14:18,541
And when are all the passengers
supposed to wake up?

172
00:14:18,565 --> 00:14:20,400
Not till the last four months.

173
00:14:21,485 --> 00:14:23,570
How is it that I'm sitting here with you

174
00:14:24,112 --> 00:14:25,822
with 90 years to go?

175
00:14:30,285 --> 00:14:31,787
It's not possible for you to be here.

176
00:14:34,748 --> 00:14:36,208
Well, I am.

177
00:14:41,004 --> 00:14:43,548
Good morning.
It's a beautiful day here on the avalon.

178
00:14:43,799 --> 00:14:46,927
So wake up, sunshine.
It's time to relax and enjoy your stay.

179
00:14:58,063 --> 00:14:59,898
