You know, you don't have to go.

807
01:09:45,430 --> 01:09:48,558
You could do
whatever it is you have to do right here.

808
01:09:50,268 --> 01:09:51,269
But...

809
01:09:51,937 --> 01:09:55,023
Since you're going, here's my wish.

810
01:09:57,317 --> 01:10:01,613
I hope you finally find someone
who fills your heart, and

811
01:10:02,280 --> 01:10:04,241
I hope you let him in.

812
01:10:05,742 --> 01:10:09,663
I hope you realize you don't have to do
something amazing to be happy.

813
01:10:12,165 --> 01:10:14,751
You know, have fun,

814
01:10:15,627 --> 01:10:17,254
take chances.

815
01:10:19,798 --> 01:10:20,924
Okay.

816
01:10:22,342 --> 01:10:23,802
I love you, Aurora.

817
01:10:24,553 --> 01:10:25,846
Bye.

818
01:10:28,765 --> 01:10:30,660
Morning, Arthur!

819
01:10:30,684 --> 01:10:32,602
- Coffee, please.
- Coming up.

820
01:10:38,650 --> 01:10:40,610
Are you soiling my barstool?

821
01:10:40,819 --> 01:10:43,113
You want to make things,
you got to get your hands dirty.

822
01:10:43,989 --> 01:10:45,157
And what have you been making?

823
01:10:45,657 --> 01:10:47,033
Improvements.

824
01:10:48,034 --> 01:10:50,036
Grand concourse.

825
01:11:17,189 --> 01:11:18,523
First floor.

826
01:11:31,745 --> 01:11:33,538
Gold-class breakfast.

827
01:11:49,805 --> 01:11:52,641
This is deck chief Gus mancuso.

828
01:11:53,266 --> 01:11:56,269
Who the hell planted a tree on my ship?

829
01:12:17,791 --> 01:12:19,626
- Who did that?
- I did.

830
01:12:20,252 --> 01:12:21,253
Who are you?

831
01:12:21,586 --> 01:12:22,587
Jim Preston.

832
01:12:24,256 --> 01:12:25,257
Aurora Lane.

833
01:12:26,091 --> 01:12:27,401
Anybody else awake?

834
01:12:27,425 --> 01:12:28,969
Just me and him.

835
01:12:29,636 --> 01:12:31,137
How far along are we?

836
01:12:31,930 --> 01:12:33,139
Eighty-eight years to go.

837
01:12:41,857 --> 01:12:43,775
Hibernation failure.

838
01:12:44,943 --> 01:12:46,754
They said that couldn't happen.

839
01:12:46,778 --> 01:12:49,990
Three people, three pod failures.

840
01:12:55,287 --> 01:12:57,956
You have no idea
how long I've been trying to get in there.

841
01:12:58,123 --> 01:13:00,434
Now that you're in, don't touch anything.

842
01:13:00,458 --> 01:13:02,019
This is where you work?

843
01:13:02,043 --> 01:13:04,296
No, this is flight crew. I'm a deck chief.

844
01:13:05,589 --> 01:13:07,716
Ops, navigation, comm.

845
01:13:10,468 --> 01:13:12,929
Unauthorized personnel.

846
01:13:13,597 --> 01:13:14,639
Sorry.

847
01:13:17,183 --> 01:13:20,413
If I'm reading this right, we're still on course.

848
01:13:20,437 --> 01:13:23,207
So whatever's wrong with the ship,
navcom is still on the job.

849
01:13:23,231 --> 01:13:24,524
There's something wrong with the ship?

850
01:13:24,774 --> 01:13:27,253
Three pod failures?
Yeah, there's something wrong.

851
01:13:27,277 --> 01:13:29,029
Question is what.

852
01:13:31,740 --> 01:13:33,301
That's strange.

853
01:13:33,325 --> 01:13:35,970
We should be getting diagnostics
from all over the ship right here,

854
01:13:35,994 --> 01:13:37,829
but there's no data.

855
01:13:39,748 --> 01:13:41,374
Got to check all the systems manually.

856
01:13:41,499 --> 01:13:43,644
Can't we turn the ship around,
go back to earth?

857
01:13:43,668 --> 01:13:45,062
No, we're doing 50% of light speed.

858
01:13:45,086 --> 01:13:47,440
Turning back would
take just as much time as going on.

859
01:13:47,464 --> 01:13:49,275
Well, there's got to be something we can do.

860
01:13:49,299 --> 01:13:51,676
Sorry. We're going where we're going.

861
01:13:54,220 --> 01:13:55,221
You okay?

862
01:13:56,556 --> 01:13:58,326
Hibernation hangover.

863
01:13:58,350 --> 01:14:00,018
Get it all the time.

864
01:14:00,352 --> 01:14:02,204
Grand concourse.

865
01:14:02,228 --> 01:14:03,497
Two years?

866
01:14:03,521 --> 01:14:05,499
Any more trees I need to know about?

867
01:14:05,523 --> 01:14:06,524
Look out!

868
01:14:11,863 --> 01:14:13,382
Never seen that before.

869
01:14:13,406 --> 01:14:15,343
These robots have been breaking down.

870
01:14:15,367 --> 01:14:17,994
This guy makes fifteen?

871
01:14:18,662 --> 01:14:19,764
Fifteen.

872
01:14:19,788 --> 01:14:21,307
The breakfast bar went crazy today.

873
01:14:21,331 --> 01:14:23,684
- Yeah, and an elevator.
- Last week, my door broke.

874
01:14:23,708 --> 01:14:25,919
- I was trapped in my cabin for two days.
- You were?

875
01:14:27,379 --> 01:14:29,839
Things like that don't happen.
Not on this ship.

876
01:14:30,715 --> 01:14:32,759
There are 16 of these tech stations
on every deck.

877
01:14:33,760 --> 01:14:34,886
Dock your slate.

878
01:14:35,637 --> 01:14:37,156
Data syncs automatically. Got it?

879
01:14:37,180 --> 01:14:38,890
- Yeah.
- Okay.

880
01:14:39,057 --> 01:14:41,452
You take decks one and two.
You take decks three and four.

881
01:14:41,476 --> 01:14:45,397
I'm going down to the hibernation bay,
check our pods.

882
01:14:46,022 --> 01:14:47,565
Well, that should be interesting.

883
01:14:58,284 --> 01:14:59,703
Ain't you supposed to be
making your rounds?

884
01:15:01,204 --> 01:15:02,455
I'm finished.

885
01:15:05,166 --> 01:15:06,876
I checked your pod.

886
01:15:07,836 --> 01:15:10,523
Problem's very simple.
The clock chip's burnt out.

887
01:15:10,547 --> 01:15:13,359
It ain't supposed to happen,
but pretty simple.

888
01:15:13,383 --> 01:15:14,944
My pod's more complicated.

889
01:15:14,968 --> 01:15:17,905
Bunch of system failures that
all happened at the same time.

890
01:15:17,929 --> 01:15:19,764
Whole damn thing went haywire.

891
01:15:22,100 --> 01:15:23,935
Explains why I'm feeling so bad.

892
01:15:24,310 --> 01:15:25,603
But Aurora's pod...

893
01:15:29,816 --> 01:15:31,401
You did this.

894
01:15:33,820 --> 01:15:34,880
Yeah.

895
01:15:34,904 --> 01:15:37,425
All this time, I'm thinking
you're one lucky son of a bitch

896
01:15:37,449 --> 01:15:39,075
to get stuck with Aurora.

897
01:15:42,495 --> 01:15:44,414
It wasn't luck, was it?

898
01:15:44,956 --> 01:15:46,017
No.

899
01:15:46,041 --> 01:15:47,125
She knows?

900
01:15:47,834 --> 01:15:48,960
She knows.

901
01:15:51,171 --> 01:15:52,380
How long were you alone?

902
01:15:52,964 --> 01:15:54,299
A year.

903
01:15:57,969 --> 01:15:59,304
Still...

904
01:16:01,139 --> 01:16:02,640
Damn.

905
01:16:08,438 --> 01:16:10,065
Data received.

906
01:16:14,027 --> 01:16:15,278
Data received.

907
01:16:20,158 --> 01:16:22,261
- Data received.
- Same as Jim's.

908
01:16:22,285 --> 01:16:23,554
Interpolating data.

909
01:16:23,578 --> 01:16:25,639
System shutdowns...

910
01:16:25,663 --> 01:16:27,957
Everywhere, but no apparent connection.

911
01:16:29,918 --> 01:16:31,294
You saw the hibernation pods?

912
01:16:32,337 --> 01:16:33,379
I saw them.

913
01:16:34,589 --> 01:16:35,691
Data received.

914
01:16:35,715 --> 01:16:37,008
So you know

915
01:16:38,343 --> 01:16:39,344
what Jim did.

916
01:16:42,347 --> 01:16:43,681
Yeah.

917
01:16:44,474 --> 01:16:45,475
And?

918
01:16:46,059 --> 01:16:48,394
- It's not my...
- He woke me up.

919
01:16:49,062 --> 01:16:50,498
He took away my life.

920
01:16:50,522 --> 01:16:52,666
I know, and I'm sorry, but there's work I'd...

921
01:16:52,690 --> 01:16:54,442
It's murder.

922
01:16:57,362 --> 01:16:58,964
You're right, Aurora.

923
01:16:58,988 --> 01:17:02,676
But the drowning man will always try
and drag somebody down with him.

924
01:17:02,700 --> 01:17:05,328
It ain't right, but the man's drowning.

925
01:17:07,372 --> 01:17:09,040
This one makes 16.

926
01:17:15,964 --> 01:17:17,674
Hey. You okay?

927
01:17:20,426 --> 01:17:22,929
- You should go rest.
- Yeah.

928
01:17:23,680 --> 01:17:28,059
But just a couple hours,
and then back at it first thing in the morning.

929
01:20:15,226 --> 01:20:16,870
I was in the pool when the gravity gave out.

930
01:20:16,894 --> 01:20:18,038
Are you okay?

931
01:20:18,062 --> 01:20:19,731
We need to find Gus.

932
01:20:21,232 --> 01:20:22,942
Gus! Gus!

933
01:20:23,943 --> 01:20:27,172
Gravity loss means that whatever's wrong
is starting to hit the big-ticket items.

934
01:20:27,196 --> 01:20:28,448
Not good.

935
01:20:29,324 --> 01:20:31,051
Every failure's a burnt out processor.

936
01:20:31,075 --> 01:20:33,828
Everything on board's thinking too hard.

937
01:20:34,370 --> 01:20:35,580
Why?

938
01:20:36,414 --> 01:20:39,143
Computer, display these failures over time.

939
01:20:39,167 --> 01:20:41,294
Processing timeline.

940
01:20:42,545 --> 01:20:44,088
Cascade failure.

941
01:20:45,173 --> 01:20:47,592
It started two years ago. Power surge.

942
01:20:48,551 --> 01:20:50,720
Seventeen failures in one day.

943
01:20:51,471 --> 01:20:53,598
Including hibernation pod 1498.

944
01:20:53,723 --> 01:20:54,766
That's me.

945
01:20:55,433 --> 01:20:56,893
Woke me up.

946
01:20:58,519 --> 01:21:01,064
- What happened that day?
- Something big.

947
01:21:01,189 --> 01:21:03,316
A major system went down somewhere.

948
01:21:03,816 --> 01:21:06,128
Everything else on board
is trying to pick up the load,

949
01:21:06,152 --> 01:21:07,921
but the load's too heavy.

950
01:21:07,945 --> 01:21:09,781
Whatever started this, we got to find it.

951
01:21:09,947 --> 01:21:11,050
And fix it.

952
01:21:11,074 --> 01:21:12,408
How bad can this get?

953
01:21:13,785 --> 01:21:16,055
Give me risk analysis based on this data.

954
01:21:16,079 --> 01:21:17,121
Extrapolating.

955
01:21:17,705 --> 01:21:20,392
A mission-critical failure is imminent.

956
01:21:20,416 --> 01:21:23,437
Failing systems.
Life support, fusion reactor...

957
01:21:23,461 --> 01:21:24,646
So we're stranded.

958
01:21:24,670 --> 01:21:26,690
Hibernation bay, ion drive...

959
01:21:26,714 --> 01:21:28,216
On a sinking ship.

960
01:21:37,225 --> 01:21:39,119
Main engineering.

961
01:21:39,143 --> 01:21:42,021
Not a lot of things big enough
to hit this ship that hard.

962
01:21:45,066 --> 01:21:47,735
With diagnostics out,
we'll have to find it ourselves.

963
01:21:48,486 --> 01:21:49,946
Where do we start?

964
01:21:50,822 --> 01:21:52,365
Gus!

965
01:21:55,701 --> 01:21:58,496
Scan complete. Analyzing data.

966
01:22:02,834 --> 01:22:04,419
What's it say is wrong with me?

967
01:22:04,752 --> 01:22:06,480
It's a few things.

968
01:22:06,504 --> 01:22:08,131
612 disorders found.

969
01:22:09,257 --> 01:22:10,508
Get me out of here.

970
01:22:25,231 --> 01:22:26,750
What's the prognosis?

971
01:22:26,774 --> 01:22:30,069
Critical diagnoses cannot be discussed
without a doctor in attendance.

972
01:22:31,112 --> 01:22:35,217
Override on my authority. ID 2317.

973
01:22:35,241 --> 01:22:36,552
Lay it on me, doc.

974
01:22:36,576 --> 01:22:38,369
Pansystemic necrosis.

975
01:22:38,536 --> 01:22:41,164
Progressive organ failure. Cause, unknown.

976
01:22:41,539 --> 01:22:43,708
My goofy hibernation pod. That's the cause.

977
01:22:44,250 --> 01:22:47,312
- What's the treatment?
- Various treatments are possible.

978
01:22:47,336 --> 01:22:49,547
None will meaningfully extend
the patient's life.

979
01:22:53,509 --> 01:22:54,695
How long have I got?

980
01:22:54,719 --> 01:22:57,263
Your end-of-life transition
is already underway.

981
01:22:58,890 --> 01:23:02,810
These sedatives will alleviate your suffering
during these final hours.

982
01:23:20,495 --> 01:23:21,913
Gus.

983
01:23:26,751 --> 01:23:28,377
I need a minute.

984
01:23:58,157 --> 01:24:01,094
We are experiencing difficulties in flight.

985
01:24:01,118 --> 01:24:03,096
- Gus!
- Gus!

986
01:24:03,120 --> 01:24:04,264
Where could he be?

987
01:24:04,288 --> 01:24:07,166
For your own safety,
please return to your cabins.

988
01:24:11,128 --> 01:24:14,024
We are experiencing difficulties in flight.

989
01:24:14,048 --> 01:24:17,593
For your own safety,
please return to your cabins.

990
01:24:17,760 --> 01:24:19,512
Should've took the damn pills.

991
01:24:20,346 --> 01:24:23,015
- I'll go get them.
- No. Stay here with me.

992
01:24:24,475 --> 01:24:26,227
Sit down.

993
01:24:30,565 --> 01:24:32,650
You two take care of each other.

994
01:24:42,159 --> 01:24:43,578
My ID.

995
01:24:45,413 --> 01:24:47,873
Get you where you need to go.

996
01:24:49,000 --> 01:24:50,751
Fix the ship.

997
01:24:51,919 --> 01:24:54,005
Find out what's wrong with her.

998
01:24:57,258 --> 01:24:58,509
How do I look?

999
01:24:59,719 --> 01:25:01,512
You look magnificent.

1000
01:25:02,555 --> 01:25:04,640
Ladies love the dress blues.

1001
01:25:14,191 --> 01:25:15,276
What do we do now?

1002
01:25:22,783 --> 01:25:24,076
This can't be good.

1003
01:25:27,496 --> 01:25:29,224
I'm going back to engineering.

1004
01:25:29,248 --> 01:25:30,791
Can you fix this?

1005
01:25:31,375 --> 01:25:32,877
I need your help.

1006
01:25:35,921 --> 01:25:36,922
Let's go.

1007
01:25:59,862 --> 01:26:00,905
Arthur!

1008
01:26:16,379 --> 01:26:17,380
Let's go.

1009
01:26:21,550 --> 01:26:23,528
Main engineering.

1010
01:26:23,552 --> 01:26:25,572
Can't we wake up some of the crew?

1011
01:26:25,596 --> 01:26:27,991
It'll take them too long to recover.
We don't have that kind of time.

1012
01:26:28,015 --> 01:26:29,433
What are we even looking for?

1013
01:26:30,226 --> 01:26:33,229
Something broken. Something big.

1014
01:26:34,230 --> 01:26:35,523
Come on.

1015
01:26:37,274 --> 01:26:38,335
Is it broken?

1016
01:26:38,359 --> 01:26:40,587
It seems okay. What's next?

1017
01:26:40,611 --> 01:26:42,947
Power plant. This way.

1018
01:26:48,744 --> 01:26:50,454
Come on.

1019
01:26:50,788 --> 01:26:52,373
The whole section's closed off.
Something's wrong.

1020
01:26:52,498 --> 01:26:54,101
We're looking for wrong.

1021
01:26:54,125 --> 01:26:55,126
Try to open it.

1022
01:27:07,346 --> 01:27:10,117
Warning. Pressure fault.

1023
01:27:10,141 --> 01:27:12,059
Lockdown initiated.

1024
01:27:15,229 --> 01:27:18,357
- Please secure all doors.
- Hold on!

1025
01:27:20,985 --> 01:27:23,630
Warning. Dangerous oxygen level.

1026
01:27:23,654 --> 01:27:25,614
Please secure all doors.

1027
01:27:35,458 --> 01:27:37,310
Dangerous oxygen level.

1028
01:27:37,334 --> 01:27:39,420
Please secure all doors.

1029
01:27:43,674 --> 01:27:44,925
Grab it!

1030
01:27:51,807 --> 01:27:54,727
Pressurizing cabin unsuccessful.

1031
01:28:03,277 --> 01:28:04,862
Pressure normalized.

1032
01:28:06,071 --> 01:28:07,924
Oxygen level restored.

1033
01:28:07,948 --> 01:28:10,010
- There's a...
- End lockdown.

1034
01:28:10,034 --> 01:28:11,869
A hole in the ship.

1035
01:28:14,497 --> 01:28:15,539
More than one.

1036
01:28:19,293 --> 01:28:22,189
How did that even happen?
The ship's supposed to be meteor-proof.

1037
01:28:22,213 --> 01:28:23,255
I guess one got through.

1038
01:28:31,514 --> 01:28:32,556
It's hot.

1039
01:28:40,022 --> 01:28:41,106
I think we found it.

1040
01:28:51,617 --> 01:28:54,078
It's the reactor-control computer.

1041
01:28:59,917 --> 01:29:01,603
This is what hit us two years ago.

1042
01:29:01,627 --> 01:29:03,003
Jim...

1043
01:29:03,546 --> 01:29:04,880
How can we fix this?

1044
01:29:08,759 --> 01:29:09,760
We're gonna die.

1045
01:29:09,885 --> 01:29:11,595
There's replacement parts for everything.

1046
01:29:16,517 --> 01:29:18,435
- Light.
- Sorry.

1047
01:29:20,771 --> 01:29:23,458
Soon as I pull this module,
the entire computer's gonna shut down.

1048
01:29:23,482 --> 01:29:25,317
Well, what happens then?

1049
01:29:26,861 --> 01:29:28,529
I'll get it back up as quickly as I can.

1050
01:29:33,284 --> 01:29:34,285
Hurry!

1051
01:29:36,954 --> 01:29:38,622
- Jim!
- Okay.

1052
01:29:41,292 --> 01:29:42,793
Control computer restored.

1053
01:29:44,753 --> 01:29:45,963
Venting reactor.

1054
01:29:48,549 --> 01:29:51,069
- But we fixed it!
- Reactor vent failed.

1055
01:29:51,093 --> 01:29:53,429
Manual override required.

1056
01:29:59,310 --> 01:30:00,370
Vent failure.

1057
01:30:00,394 --> 01:30:01,979
- Come on!
- Jim.

1058
01:30:06,901 --> 01:30:08,712
Outer door nonresponsive.

1059
01:30:08,736 --> 01:30:10,487
What does that mean?

1060
01:30:12,156 --> 01:30:14,092
The outer door is jammed.

1061
01:30:14,116 --> 01:30:16,094
We've got to open that door
and cool the reactor down,

1062
01:30:16,118 --> 01:30:17,494
or the whole ship is gonna blow.

1063
01:30:17,953 --> 01:30:20,390
- How?
- I got to go out there.

1064
01:30:20,414 --> 01:30:21,999
Open it from the outside.

1065
01:30:22,958 --> 01:30:24,501
I open the door, I get clear.

1066
01:30:25,628 --> 01:30:28,648
- You blow that fire into space.
- You get clear?

1067
01:30:28,672 --> 01:30:30,317
You can talk to me through this.

1068
01:30:30,341 --> 01:30:32,343
What happens to you when that door opens?

1069
01:30:42,853 --> 01:30:44,355
Heat shield. It might help.

1070
01:30:53,697 --> 01:30:55,240
You might need this.

1071
01:31:08,921 --> 01:31:09,922
It's gonna be okay.

1072
01:31:20,224 --> 01:31:21,308
I better go.

1073
01:31:26,647 --> 01:31:29,066
Jim. Jim.

1074
01:31:32,403 --> 01:31:33,904
Come back to me.

1075
01:31:35,614 --> 01:31:37,700
I can't live on the ship without you.

1076
01:32:03,183 --> 01:32:04,244
Warning.

1077
01:32:04,268 --> 01:32:06,061
Temperature critical.

1078
01:32:19,283 --> 01:32:20,784
What's wrong?

1079
01:32:21,285 --> 01:32:22,429
What's the matter?

1080
01:32:22,453 --> 01:32:23,972
- Are you okay?
- Nothing.

1081
01:32:23,996 --> 01:32:25,789
- Go.
- You sure?

1082
01:32:25,914 --> 01:32:27,207
Go.

1083
01:32:34,923 --> 01:32:36,008
I'm at the vent tube.

1084
01:32:37,718 --> 01:32:39,762
New anchor point. Reset tether.

1085
01:32:43,807 --> 01:32:44,933
I see the door.

1086
01:32:46,185 --> 01:32:48,062
Temperature level rising.

1087
01:32:55,277 --> 01:32:57,279
Warning. Temperature critical.

1088
01:33:04,161 --> 01:33:05,746
Containment unstable.

1089
01:33:07,623 --> 01:33:09,893
- Where are you?
- I'm at the door.

1090
01:33:09,917 --> 01:33:11,478
I'm ready. Just say when.

1091
01:33:11,502 --> 01:33:12,503
Here goes.

1092
01:33:16,215 --> 01:33:17,341
The door won't open.

1093
01:33:17,508 --> 01:33:19,176
I'll have to bypass it.

1094
01:33:21,470 --> 01:33:23,347
Temperature level rising.

1095
01:33:24,473 --> 01:33:25,599
Jim, come on!

1096
01:33:25,724 --> 01:33:27,184
Please hurry!

1097
01:33:27,559 --> 01:33:29,812
- Okay, I'm trying it again.
- Tell me when you're clear.

1098
01:33:34,691 --> 01:33:35,692
- No!
- What?

1099
01:33:37,152 --> 01:33:38,195
What's going on?

1100
01:33:39,279 --> 01:33:40,531
Jim?

1101
01:33:44,535 --> 01:33:45,577
Jim!

1102
01:33:45,911 --> 01:33:47,204
The door won't stay open.

1103
01:33:49,206 --> 01:33:50,374
I think I have to stay here.

1104
01:33:50,916 --> 01:33:52,251
Hold the door open.

1105
01:33:52,543 --> 01:33:53,603
What?

1106
01:33:53,627 --> 01:33:54,711
No!

1107
01:33:55,045 --> 01:33:56,564
No way! Get out of there!

1108
01:33:56,588 --> 01:33:58,191
I can't.

1109
01:33:58,215 --> 01:33:59,550
Jim.

1110
01:33:59,925 --> 01:34:00,926
We're out of time.

1111
01:34:02,803 --> 01:34:05,222
- Containment unstable.
- Jim?

1112
01:34:12,062 --> 01:34:13,105
Vent the reactor.

1113
01:34:20,028 --> 01:34:22,406
No! You don't understand!

1114
01:34:23,240 --> 01:34:25,927
If I open the door right now, it'll kill you!

1115
01:34:25,951 --> 01:34:26,952
I'm hoping not.

1116
01:34:27,077 --> 01:34:28,972
Come back in. We'll think of something else.

1117
01:34:28,996 --> 01:34:30,414
There is nothing else.

1118
01:34:31,832 --> 01:34:32,875
Jim!

1119
01:34:34,084 --> 01:34:35,145
- It's okay.
- No!

1120
01:34:35,169 --> 01:34:37,063
- It's not okay!
- Aurora...

1121
01:34:37,087 --> 01:34:38,881
Warning. Temperature level exceeded.

1122
01:34:39,089 --> 01:34:40,966
This isn't what you said was gonna happen!

1123
01:34:42,634 --> 01:34:44,070
Aurora, this ship is gonna go.

1124
01:34:44,094 --> 01:34:46,096
I don't care! You die, I die.

1125
01:34:47,181 --> 01:34:49,766
There are 5,000 other people
on this ship, Aurora.

1126
01:34:51,310 --> 01:34:52,394
We have to do this.

1127
01:34:53,979 --> 01:34:55,439
Maximum pressure reached.

1128
01:34:58,984 --> 01:35:01,111
Do it. Now.

1129
01:35:02,779 --> 01:35:04,907
Maximum cabin pressure reached.

1130
01:35:26,428 --> 01:35:27,888
Temperature dropping.

1131
01:35:29,473 --> 01:35:30,474
Jim.

1132
01:35:49,326 --> 01:35:51,346
- Jim?
- Vent successful.

1133
01:35:51,370 --> 01:35:53,932
Rebooting process initiated.

1134
01:35:53,956 --> 01:35:55,040
Jim, please say something.

1135
01:36:32,661 --> 01:36:34,329
Suit pressure dropping.

1136
01:36:37,666 --> 01:36:40,210
Return to ship immediately.

1137
01:36:41,253 --> 01:36:42,296
Aurora?

1138
01:36:44,798 --> 01:36:46,025
It worked!

1139
01:36:46,049 --> 01:36:47,384
You did it! You can come in!

1140
01:36:48,343 --> 01:36:50,280
Yeah, about that.

1141
01:36:50,304 --> 01:36:52,490
What's the matter? Are you hurt?

1142
01:36:52,514 --> 01:36:54,284
I got blown out of the tube.

1143
01:36:54,308 --> 01:36:56,035
- What?
- My tether broke.

1144
01:36:56,059 --> 01:36:58,228
I can't get back to the ship.

1145
01:36:58,854 --> 01:37:00,772
I'll come out. I'll come out. I'll pull you in.

1146
01:37:00,897 --> 01:37:03,525
Warning. Oxygen level critical.

1147
01:37:03,734 --> 01:37:05,819
Return to ship immediately.

1148
01:37:14,536 --> 01:37:17,080
Aurora, I'm sorry.

1149
01:37:19,082 --> 01:37:20,083
For everything.

1150
01:37:20,250 --> 01:37:22,419
Shut up. I'm coming.

1151
01:37:22,586 --> 01:37:26,590
I wish we'd have met in 90 years.

1152
01:37:31,970 --> 01:37:34,973
I'd have built you a house.

1153
01:37:39,770 --> 01:37:41,772
I'd have read your book.

1154
01:37:44,274 --> 01:37:45,609
It's gonna be great.

1155
01:37:58,205 --> 01:37:59,206
Tether attached.

1156
01:37:59,623 --> 01:38:01,333
Locate Jim Preston.

1157
01:38:06,004 --> 01:38:08,465
Jim Preston located.

1158
01:38:09,633 --> 01:38:10,967
I'm coming to get you.

1159
01:38:36,118 --> 01:38:37,494
Jim!

1160
01:39:37,387 --> 01:39:39,264
I'm sorry. The patient is dead.

1161
01:39:39,723 --> 01:39:41,576
Well, resuscitate him!

1162
01:39:41,600 --> 01:39:44,704
Postmortem operations require
authorized medical supervision.

1163
01:39:44,728 --> 01:39:46,521
No.

1164
01:39:47,147 --> 01:39:48,565
Jim.

1165
01:39:54,488 --> 01:39:55,548
Override!

1166
01:39:55,572 --> 01:39:57,049
Override on my authority!

1167
01:39:57,073 --> 01:39:59,910
ID 1-7...

1168
01:40:02,078 --> 01:40:05,391
Two... Two. Two.

1169
01:40:05,415 --> 01:40:06,583
2-3-1-7.

1170
01:40:07,083 --> 01:40:09,544
2-3-1-7! ID 2-3-1-7!

1171
01:40:13,423 --> 01:40:14,591
Resuscitation.

1172
01:40:17,761 --> 01:40:19,906
Multiple procedures are not recommended.

1173
01:40:19,930 --> 01:40:22,265
Override! Do it now!

1174
01:40:22,849 --> 01:40:24,017
Executing.

1175
01:41:20,240 --> 01:41:21,324
Hi!

1176
01:41:23,285 --> 01:41:24,286
Jim!

1177
01:41:27,122 --> 01:41:28,415
Hey, Jim.

1178
01:41:56,401 --> 01:41:58,361
You brought me back.

1179
01:41:58,778 --> 01:42:00,113
Yeah.

1180
01:42:24,346 --> 01:42:26,306
- Thank you.
- Be still.

1181
01:42:26,723 --> 01:42:27,932
Of course.

1182
01:43:13,395 --> 01:43:15,146
There's something I have to show you.

1183
01:43:15,438 --> 01:43:16,749
In command mode, it turns out

1184
01:43:16,773 --> 01:43:20,985
the autodoc has an option
called stabilize and suspend.

1185
01:43:21,444 --> 01:43:23,655
It stops all metabolic activity.

1186
01:43:25,532 --> 01:43:26,533
What are you saying?

1187
01:43:26,950 --> 01:43:30,471
With Gus's ID, it can be like hibernation
inside the autodoc.

1188
01:43:30,495 --> 01:43:31,496
You can go back to sleep.

1189
01:43:36,626 --> 01:43:38,461
But there's only one autodoc.

1190
01:43:42,966 --> 01:43:44,300
Yeah.

1191
01:43:46,469 --> 01:43:50,390
And you're gonna lay down in it
and fall asleep.

1192
01:43:51,516 --> 01:43:53,828
And you'll wake up on homestead ii.

1193
01:43:53,852 --> 01:43:55,645
And you'll write your book.

1194
01:43:57,313 --> 01:43:58,457
You'd finish your journey.

1195
01:43:58,481 --> 01:44:00,358
You'd do what you set out to do.

1196
01:44:08,992 --> 01:44:10,660
You'd be alone.

1197
01:44:11,995 --> 01:44:13,705
I've been alone before.

1198
01:44:14,247 --> 01:44:15,498
And I'll be fine.

1199
01:44:17,250 --> 01:44:19,002
But I would never see you again.

1200
01:44:22,839 --> 01:44:24,340
I'll come and visit you.

1201
01:45:07,383 --> 01:45:09,052
Tuesday is my day with Arthur.

1202
01:45:11,179 --> 01:45:12,782
Lovely as ever.

1203
01:45:12,806 --> 01:45:15,058
Thank you, Arthur.
You're looking very well yourself.

1204
01:45:15,183 --> 01:45:16,559
Thanks to you.

1205
01:45:17,560 --> 01:45:18,561
What's that?

1206
01:45:21,606 --> 01:45:23,608
Something I've wanted to give you
for a long time.

1207
01:45:30,949 --> 01:45:32,575
It's beautiful.

1208
01:45:45,588 --> 01:45:47,757
Took you long enough to ask.

1209
01:45:50,844 --> 01:45:52,262
Champagne.

1210
01:45:52,846 --> 01:45:53,888
I'll wait.

1211
01:46:11,155 --> 01:46:12,949
Hell of a life.

1212
01:46:15,451 --> 01:46:16,953
Hell of a life.

1213
01:46:48,234 --> 01:46:51,821
Crew wake-up process initiated.

1214
01:46:52,447 --> 01:46:54,383
My fellow passengers,

1215
01:46:54,407 --> 01:46:55,885
if you're reading this,

1216
01:46:55,909 --> 01:46:59,722
then the starship avalon
has reached its destination.

1217
01:46:59,746 --> 01:47:02,099
Grand concourse.

1218
01:47:02,123 --> 01:47:03,958
A lot happened while you slept.

1219
01:47:11,633 --> 01:47:13,569
A friend once said,

1220
01:47:13,593 --> 01:47:16,739
"you can't get so hung up
on where you'd rather be

1221
01:47:16,763 --> 01:47:19,849
that you forget to make
the most of where you are.”

1222
01:47:20,850 --> 01:47:22,894
We got lost along the way.

1223
01:47:23,895 --> 01:47:25,563
But we found each other.

1224
01:47:26,356 --> 01:47:28,125
And we made a life.

1225
01:47:28,149 --> 01:47:30,276
A beautiful life.

1226
01:47:30,693 --> 01:47:32,362
Together.

